WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.234
Week 29: Relative Clauses and Unknown Referents. define a requirement identify known and unknown people or things connect complex information

2
00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:24.737
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can define a requirement, identify known and unknown people or things, connect complex information. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:33.563
Language system. Relative pronouns; indicative versus subjunctive in adjective clauses; lo que, quien, el que, and cuyo.

4
00:00:33.563 --> 00:00:39.723
Sound and delivery. Long sentence phrasing with audible relative-clause boundaries.

5
00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:49.149
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:49.149 --> 00:01:18.991
Model language. Buscamos a alguien que tenga experiencia. — We are looking for someone who has experience. Conozco a la persona que dirige el proyecto. — I know the person who directs the project. Necesito un lugar que esté cerca del metro. — I need a place that is near the subway. Eso es lo que me preocupa. — That is what worries me. La autora, cuyo libro ganó el premio, dará una charla. — The author whose book won the prize will give a talk.

7
00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:28.910
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
